# Build context for the container image.
#
# The image builds the storefront from `web/` (the Dockerfile's first stage),
# so the app sources and the lockfile must be IN here — they used to be
# excluded, back when the image expected a pre-built `web/out` copied in from
# the build machine. What stays out is what the container never runs:
# host-built `node_modules`, the dev server's `.next`, the live data dir, the
# retired paths under `archive/`, and the decision/capture/docs material that
# is not code.
.git
.gitignore
.commandcode
archive
container
decisions
deploy
docs
examples
games
p2
p3
research
scripts

# the provider catalog ships; its fetch caches are machine state
probes/*cache*.json

web/node_modules
web/.next
web/out
web/README.md
demo/data

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
*.md